From c1267464b72d232dd9bc9e28059ad0d9e271ab89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:37:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(pm): real-bootstrap relaunch test survives the bootstrap
 preload

Release CI run 40649515376 (main bcf47021db) shard 1 failed all 3 params
of test_real_bootstrap_reexecs_before_app_imports: the re-exec'd child
died with "No module named 'pm'" at hermes_bootstrap.py:577. Red locally
on main, 26 passed with this change (with test_borrowed_home_launch.py).

Five whys:
1. Why red? The re-exec'd child imported pm before anything put the
   repository on sys.path.
2. Why? bcf47021db makes relaunch_command load <root>/hermes_bootstrap.py
   before the entry, so the bootstrap's `from pm.environments import ...`
   now runs first.
3. Why does that fail only here? This test's disposable source root holds
   just a copied bootstrap; the repository path and the acquisition fakes
   came from launch_test_tools, which the entry imported first. Real
   installs ship pm/ in the root, so the product path is fine.
4. Why not caught? bcf47021db ran its own borrowed-home tests; this file
   needs real uv and was not in that run.
5. Fix: the copied bootstrap imports launch_test_tools right after its
   __future__ line, so every load (entry or relaunch preload) sees the
   same path and fakes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/pm/test_source_update_launch.py | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/pm/test_source_update_launch.py b/tests/pm/test_source_update_launch.py
index 7d16ba8be1..c14d57b248 100644
--- a/tests/pm/test_source_update_launch.py
+++ b/tests/pm/test_source_update_launch.py
@@ -369,7 +369,15 @@ def test_real_bootstrap_reexecs_before_app_imports(source_launch, tmp_path, isol
     repository = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
     # Copy the real bootstrap so it owns this disposable source install. The
     # other modules remain real checkout imports; only acquisition is injected.
-    shutil.copy2(repository / "hermes_bootstrap.py", root / "hermes_bootstrap.py")
+    # A relaunch loads the bootstrap before the entry (relaunch_command), and this
+    # root has no pm/ of its own, so the copy imports the test tools itself.
+    bootstrap = (repository / "hermes_bootstrap.py").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    future = "from __future__ import annotations\n"
+    assert future in bootstrap
+    (root / "hermes_bootstrap.py").write_text(
+        bootstrap.replace(future, future + "import launch_test_tools  # noqa: E402,F401\n", 1),
+        encoding="utf-8",
+    )
     (root / "launch_test_tools.py").write_text(
         "import sys\n"
         "from pathlib import Path\n"
